Yeah, I've got that in IDA as:

```c++
  memset(wCityInventionYears, 0, 0x20u);
  wCityInventionYears[16] = 0;
```

The actual grunt work that the new city dialog does for setting the invention years in the first place:

```c++
  while ( 1 )
  {
    v1 = (unsigned __int16)rand() % 20u + wBaseInventionYears[v0];
    wCityInventionYears[v0] = v1;
    if ( v1 < wCityStartYear )
      wCityInventionYears[v0] = 0;
    if ( ++v0 >= 17 )
      // a bunch of other stuff not relevant to the above happens here for some reason
      break;
  }
```
